Good to know:title.template applies to child route segments and not the segment it's defined in. This means:title.default is required when you add a title.template.title.template defined in layout.js will not apply to a title defined in a page.js of the same route segment.title.template defined in page.js has no effect because a page is always the terminating segment (it doesn't have any children route segments).title.template has no effect if a route has not defined a title or title.default.

